# Agon 08_sand_casualpirates layers 6+7 (met2, run 2): the latch-driven arms. statecall runs a
# state body directly, so the sequence of AttachToTarget / DetachFromTarget calls is deterministic:
# a second metroid attacking a player that already holds one (AttachToTarget false), the morphed
# detach, and a pirate detach (the pirate's branch of DetachFromTarget), plus GetOrigin with a
# player target in both morph states and with the metroid exactly on the player (zero direction).
@f300 layer 6
@f340 layer 7
@f560 god 1; give morphBall 1; give morphBallBombs 1; give powerBombs 5; fastmorph 1; give missile 20
@f580 send u0547 Activate; send u053d Activate; send u0539 Activate; send u0538 Activate; send u0535 Activate
@f600 objs metroid
@f620 objs pirate

# SelectTarget: One -> Two with a target (the SetTargetVector arm).
@f700 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f720 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f760 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1
@f800 statecall u0547 SelectTarget 1

# AttachToTarget: u0547 takes the player, then u0538's Attack cannot (the player already holds one).
@f900 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f920 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 Attack
@f950 obj u0547
@f980 place u0538 player 2; fsm u0538 SelectTarget
@f1000 statecall u0538 Attack 0
@f1020 obj u0538

# DetachFromTarget with the player morphed (the quaternion arm), then back to unmorphed.
@f1100 press x 4
@f1200 obj u0547; status
@f1300 statecall u0547 Attack 2
@f1400 obj u0547; status
@f1450 press x 4

# DetachFromTarget on a pirate: u0539 latches u04d8, then u053d's Attack finds the pirate taken
# (PreDamageSpacePirate's IsPirateValidTarget false), then u0539 leaves (the pirate branch).
@f1500 place u0539 366 -279 3
@f1520 fsm u0539 SelectTarget
@f1560 fsm u0539 Attack
@f1600 obj u0539
@f1620 objs pirate
@f1660 place u053d 366 -279 3; fsm u053d SelectTarget
@f1700 statecall u053d Attack 0
@f1720 obj u053d
@f1800 statecall u0539 Attack 2
@f1850 obj u0539

# GetOrigin with a player target: unmorphed, then morphed, then the metroid exactly on the player
# (the zero-direction arm), then unmorphed again.
@f1900 place u0547 player 2; fsm u0547 SelectTarget
@f2000 press x 4
@f2100 place u0547 player 0
@f2200 obj u0547; status
@f2300 place u0547 player 0
@f2400 press x 4
@f2500 place u0547 player 2
@f2600 obj u0547; status

# SwarmRemove / death paths: a metroid with no team manager, then the team members' Delete.
@f2700 kill u0535
@f2800 send u0538 Deactivate
@f2900 kill u0538
@f3000 send u0547 Deactivate
@f3100 obj u0547; status
